From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Prussin <cprussin@bci-incorporated.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:38:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: reach the broker from outside, and prove viz
 aggregates

Step 2 of the spike in docs/architecture/ENGINE-FORK.md. Adds the throwaway
half: content/browser/domicile/domicile_spike.{h,cc}, which opens a
NamedPlatformChannel and sends a real mojo invitation carrying the step-1
FrameSinkBroker plus a stand-in embedder, and
components/domicile/spike/, the external producer that submits solid-colour
CompositorFrames to it.

The two edits to files Chromium owns are the source list and dep in
content/browser/BUILD.gn, and one call in browser_main_loop.cc. The call is in
PostCreateThreads rather than PreMainMessageLoopRun because
PostCreateThreadsImpl() is what creates the ImageTransportFactory the broker
takes its HostFrameSinkManager from, and because Chrome does not return from
parts_->PreMainMessageLoopRun() in time to be useful.

All of it is a no-op without --domicile-broker-socket.
---
 content/browser/BUILD.gn             | 5 ++++-
 content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/BUILD.gn b/content/browser/BUILD.gn
index 0bab55e691d6c..857721a48ced4 100644
--- a/content/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/content/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -150,8 +150,9 @@ source_set("browser") {
     "//components/cbor",
     "//components/discardable_memory/common",
     "//components/discardable_memory/service",
-    "//components/download/database",
     "//components/domicile:browser",
+    "//components/domicile/spike/mojom",
+    "//components/download/database",
     "//components/download/public/common:public",
     "//components/embedder_support",
     "//components/embedder_support:user_agent",
@@ -936,6 +937,8 @@ source_set("browser") {
     "dom_storage/session_storage_namespace_impl.h",
     "domicile/domicile_frame_sink_broker.cc",
     "domicile/domicile_frame_sink_broker.h",
+    "domicile/domicile_spike.cc",
+    "domicile/domicile_spike.h",
     "download/data_url_blob_reader.cc",
     "download/data_url_blob_reader.h",
     "download/download_item_utils.cc",
diff --git a/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc b/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
index 90d60c44cc235..4306ea8cfc150 100644
--- a/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
+++ b/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 #include "content/browser/browser_thread_impl.h"
 #include "content/browser/compositor/viz_process_transport_factory.h"
 #include "content/browser/cpu_performance/cpu_performance.h"
+#include "content/browser/domicile/domicile_spike.h"
 #include "content/browser/download/save_file_manager.h"
 #include "content/browser/field_trial_synchronizer.h"
 #include "content/browser/first_party_sets/first_party_set_parser.h"
@@ -1038,6 +1039,11 @@ int BrowserMainLoop::PostCreateThreads() {
 
   PostCreateThreadsImpl();
 
+  // Throwaway; step 2 of the spike. A no-op without --domicile-broker-socket.
+  // Here rather than later because PostCreateThreadsImpl() is what creates the
+  // ImageTransportFactory the broker takes its HostFrameSinkManager from.
+  MaybeStartDomicileSpike();
+
   return result_code_;
 }
 
